    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d269">

                <pb facs="0433" n="333" sameAs="frus:frus1934v02/pg333"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">862.51/3782</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the British
                        Ambassador</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lindsay</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-12-29">December 29, 1933</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your Excellency’s note of December 23, 1933, informing me of the
                    communication made by your Government to the German Government in regard to
                    treatment of German foreign loans.</p>
                <p>This Government has instructed its representative at Berlin to make formal
                    representations to the German Government in the same sense, and has instructed
                    that representative in general to support the position outlined in your
                    note.</p>
                <p>This Government will be glad to be kept informed of any further developments
                    which come to the attention of the British Government and to continue the effort
                    of common representation and activity in this matter.</p>
                <p>Accept, [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">William Phillips</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
